{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"cbaac3bcf3f9ffb6","type":"text","text":"Returns all creatures from the board to their summoner's hands, or destroys ones that are transient.","x":-214,"y":-264,"width":280,"height":119},
		{"id":"25d55c50057641d2","type":"text","text":"Reduces opponent's mana gain per turn by 1. Can go no lower than 1.","x":-214,"y":-112,"width":250,"height":85},
		{"id":"ba80b638101d4b06","type":"text","text":"Decadence: Common Ritual","x":-610,"y":-105,"width":212,"height":70},
		{"id":"dad762371a80aa7a","type":"text","text":"Cast: choose a Ritual and add a duplicate of it to your hand.","x":-214,"y":146,"width":250,"height":94},
		{"id":"3205afc8ed8cd0a1","type":"text","text":"Scribe: Common Creature","x":-610,"y":160,"width":190,"height":67},
		{"id":"3060d95c2f454c3e","type":"text","text":"Tumult Vanitas: Ritual","x":-611,"y":300,"width":191,"height":55},
		{"id":"046049b2074e4c7d","type":"text","text":"Noise Trap: Buff. When the opponent summons a creature, it costs 1 extra mana. Then Noise Trap is removed.","x":120,"y":265,"width":280,"height":130},
		{"id":"d99ecc181aa9f7ae","type":"text","text":"In Ashk'lan, the golden city of river deltas, astromancers are feared almost more than the King's men. Once hired from among the eastern defector-magi, the astromancers taught the City literacy, mathematics, and astronomy. Most citizens have never seen a living astromancer—but they say that even the King himself doesn't know all their secrets. Their knowledge, after all, is forbidden to the uninitiated; this state of things cannot be changed, either by death or what comes after. The astromancers have now withdrawn from the court and rarely come to pay their respects. In their gaunt ivory towers, they create bookish learning on parchment, returning in their minds to the origins of the world. Their gods, they say, are hidden far beyond the realm of things...","x":140,"y":-264,"width":720,"height":260},
		{"id":"ed3f83f8e4a7ec07","type":"text","text":"The Astromancers all divide in 4 sects, each governing its own cardinal direction, and each being privy to the stars of their part of the sky. To infringe on this division is to accept excommunication and lose all memories. Each sect has its own visions of the future, which shape their way of life, from Sinistrals, who channel the worst of omens, to good-natured Australs, whose visions are always auspicious.","x":140,"y":12,"width":720,"height":181},
		{"id":"b72a01c646dcbdab","type":"text","text":"Regress: Rare Ritual","x":-611,"y":-239,"width":191,"height":70},
		{"id":"4400eedeb4f0e210","type":"text","text":"On turn: gain 1 Sand. Cast: Use up all Sand and gain +1/1 for each. Then the Upright Clepsydra is unequipped.","x":-214,"y":410,"width":250,"height":150},
		{"id":"1b34500f0e989905","type":"text","text":"Upright Clepsydra: Rare Item","x":-615,"y":450,"width":195,"height":70},
		{"id":"26e75b2998df61ad","type":"text","text":"On turn: gain 1 Sand. Cast: pay 2 Sand, gain 1 Benediction and lose all Sand.","x":-214,"y":600,"width":250,"height":120},
		{"id":"dc625ae0caaab548","type":"text","text":"Austal: Rare Creature","x":-607,"y":621,"width":180,"height":78},
		{"id":"8cdb7fc4336ca74f","type":"text","text":"Benediction: player Buff. The next creature the player summons costs no Mana. Then Benediction is removed.","x":120,"y":600,"width":280,"height":120},
		{"id":"dff8de7c9b662dcf","type":"text","text":"Main Mechanics: Time Magic, Attrition, Player Damage\nWeaknesses: Situational effects.","x":-460,"y":-420,"width":304,"height":120},
		{"id":"900dc441d4be1259","type":"text","text":"In secret from everybody, Astromancers keep in contact with the Starwalkers, a flightly race from the realm of night. (Space elves?)","x":737,"y":383,"width":463,"height":102},
		{"id":"a934688f8cca83b9","type":"text","text":"Starwalker Scout","x":500,"y":600,"width":180,"height":60},
